msgid "Inputs to the Motors Library"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-copter-motors-library.rst:36
#: b57e6eebffcb4a2cb177e975d31bf973
msgid "The Attitude Controller provides high level roll, pitch, yaw and throttle commands to the Motors library in the range of -1 to +1 (for roll, pitch and yaw) or 0 to +1 (for throttle).  The exact point where the attitude controller issues these commands can be found in AC_AttitudeControl_Multi's `rate_controller_run() <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AC_AttitudeControl/AC_AttitudeControl_Multi.cpp#L253>`__ method"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-copter-motors-library.rst:48
#: 356785d2a59941058b3f064deb0225e9
msgid "and the definitions of the methods used can be seen in `AP_Motors_Class.h <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Motors/AP_Motors_Class.h#L78>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-copter-motors-library.rst:59
#: 28115743e55d4e30bac60fff16a09da5
msgid "Outputs and Responsibilities"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-copter-motors-library.rst:61
#: 15b9015aa889438a889f617485735b5e
msgid "All motors libraries must do two things:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-copter-motors-library.rst:63
#: 98549abfabb34b22b7537e46f16486f8
msgid "Convert the high level inputs from the attitude controller to individual motor and servo outputs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-copter-motors-library.rst:65
#: 3675d05c10b54ad891119b7c93974a82
msgid "Roll input of +1.0 should cause motor and servo outputs that provide maximum roll rotation to the right"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-copter-motors-library.rst:66
#: f6a7960a2cdb460899a68d2435d8dd1a
msgid "Pitch input of +1.0 should result in maximum pitch back"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-copter-motors-library.rst:67
#: eec852af1a0e4b698723ffc126e2d51a
msgid "Yaw input of +1.0 should result in maximum yaw in the clockwise direction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-copter-motors-library.rst:68
#: dee4ff6b1a8f40a89a5d77b540bdef1d
msgid "Throttle input of +1.0 should result in maximum acceleration upwards (in the vehicle's body frame).  Throttle of zero should result in minimum acceleration upwards (or maximum acceleration downwards in the case of helicopters)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-copter-motors-library.rst:70
#: fbf1d24dd9564380ac7ecb05df697e28
msgid "Set the limit flags to avoid \"I-term build-up\" in the attitude and throttle controllers.  Although a vehicle will be flyable without setting these flags, they are important for protecting against overshoot in lean angle control and also for automatic landing detection.  The limits are held in the `AP_Motors_Class::limit <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Motors/AP_Motors_Class.h#L118>`__ variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-copter-motors-library.rst:83
#: a6dada62122d40a593374f84436faac1
msgid "Adding support for a new \"Multicopter Matrix\" frame"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-copter-motors-library.rst:85
#: 8cf978f2c9f24f03bd9be72d15cf2887
msgid "To add support for a new Multicopter Matrix frame type (i.e. a frame with downward facing propellers and no servos):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-copter-motors-library.rst:87
#: 00720670b56948549229aefd22cbd629
msgid "Decide on a name for the frame and add a new entry into either the motor_frame_class and/or motor_frame_type enums found in `AP_Motors/AP_Motors_Class.h <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Motors/AP_Motors_Class.h#L32>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-copter-motors-library.rst:88
#: c578e59fe97c4b8db8489df82c187d59
msgid "Add the same number(s) from the above step to the `FRAME_CLASS <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/Parameters.cpp#L848>`__ and/or `FRAME_TYPE <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/Parameters.cpp#L361>`__ parameters descriptions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-copter-motors-library.rst:89
#: b814ae7be5764dee901e74a45c8b6848
msgid "Add a new case to the `AP_MotorsMatrix::setup_motors() <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Motors/AP_MotorsMatrix.cpp#L466>`__ for the new frame class and/or frame type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-copter-motors-library.rst:91
#: 133a65b5f5d7430ebecd30b7ae8ad5de
msgid "Use AP_MotorsMatrix::add_motor() or `AP_MotorsMatrix::add_motor_raw() <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Motors/AP_MotorsMatrix.h#L62>`__ functions to set the roll, pitch and yaw factors for each motor on the vehicle.  These factors are multiplied by the high level roll, pitch and yaw input from the attitude controllers and the result is then output to the motors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-copter-motors-library.rst:92
#: 00417bed9d8c4738b5bb10de779f8f53
msgid "The above add_motor function's testing_order argument specifies the order in which the motors should spin when the user initiates a motor test.  Normally each motor's testing order should be relative to its position on the frame in a clockwise direction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-copter-motors-library.rst:93
#: bc9c8afd6e3e484bb5232732440cf9fb
msgid "set success = true at the bottom of the case to alert the AP_Motors initialisation code that the frame has been setup"
msgstr ""

